autonomic function testing, thermoregulatory sweat test and/or
quantitative sudomotor axon reflex testing, microneurography,
measurement of supine and standing plasma norepinephrine
levels and cutaneous biopsy in selected cases. Participants
had no dietary restrictions during the days before the study,
but had nil by mouth after midnight. All vasoactive and
psychotropic medication was stopped at least five half-lives
prior to testing.

(HR) increment of 30 beats per minute (bpm) or more within
10 min of standing or head-up tilt (HUT) in the absence of
